{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499343-powersmiths-forge-masters-23-conversion-soul-forgers-optional-death-sub-legacy","id":1499343,"title":"Powersmiths (Forge Masters 23 conversion) + Soul Forgers (optional Death sub legacy)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-10T19:42:48-08:00","id":1499343,"title":"Powersmiths (Forge Masters 23 conversion) + Soul Forgers (optional Death sub legacy)","content":"<u><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forge Masters</span></span></span></b></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Powersmiths</span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pages 72-80 of Legacies: The Ancient for lore</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doctrine and Magic</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Moros </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Order: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Prime 2, Matter 1, 2 dots of Crafts, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Academics, Athletics, Occult, or Science </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiation:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Be charged with the resonance of blood, iron and fire. (See page 77 for the ful ritual)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcana:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Prime</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Yantras:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Casting a spell near a forge (+1); A piece of jewelry that the mage crafted themselves (+2); Exhaust yourself creating something (+1, +2 if it imposes a negative condition).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Smelting your own metal from ore you dug yourself; Melting down scrap metal to craft something both beautiful and useful; Repairing a weapon or armor that was damaged in battle so it\u2019s as good as new.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Attainment: Crafter\u2019s Vision</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The powersmiths must learn to identify the magical quality of objects and how they relate to their goals. This attainment functions as \u201cSupernal Vision\u201d (Prime 1, MtAw 166) with reach for instant casting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Matter 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Understanding what you are working with is essential to taking raw materials and turning them into useful tools. This attainment emulates \u201cDiscern Composition\u201d (Matter 1, MtAw 154) with reach for instant casting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second Attainment: The Master's Hand</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Prime 2, 3 dots in crafts</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The nature of their work means the forge masters prefer to have a space they can work consistently. This attainment is taught to them early on so that they may bless the places they work. The attainment functions as \u201cAs Above, So Below\u201d (Prime 2, MtAw 166) with reach for advanced duration and takes an hour of meditation in the location being blessed to activate the attainment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Matter 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The tools are just as important as the location when it comes to their work, so the forge masters also learn to bless their tools. With an hour of meditation this attainment functions as \u201cFind the Balance\u201d (Matter 2, MtAw 155) with reach for advanced duration. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third Attainment: Primal Tempering</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Prime 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The groundwork has been laid for great works to be created at the hands of the powersmith. The mage is now able to transform mana into weapons and tools to be used. This attainment takes one mana and an hour of work to activate and functions as \u201cPlatonic Form\u201d (Prime 3, MtAw 169) with reach for advanced duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Matter 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The creation of items out of mana is an impressive feat, so too is the ability to reinforce equipment that has already been made. With an hour of work powersmiths can enhance items as per the spell \u201cAegis\u201d (Matter 3, MtAw 156) with reach assigned for advanced duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth Attainment: The Flow of Mana</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Prime 4, 4 dots in crafts</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mana exists throughout the fallen world and is important to the work of the powersmiths. By this point the mage has learned how dependent they are on mana, this attainment helps them move mana where they need it, generally into themselves. This attainment functions as \u201cChannel Mana\u201d (Prime 3, MtAw 168) with reach for instant casting and to allow the mage to ignore the usual limit to their mana per turn from their gnosis, the Mage can move as much mana as they need in a moment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Matter 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every craftsman needs an assistant. While they were being tutored the now powersmith may have filled this role, but not every mage has a tutor, even those who do may need, or simply want, more help. By shaping inorganic materials for an hour the mage can create an assistant by emulating the \u201cGolem\u201d (Matter 4, MtAw 158) spell with reach for advanced duration. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth Attainment: Primal Forge</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Prime 5, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The philosophy of the forge masters is one of creation, their final attainment is the most extreme and awe inspiring example of this philosophy by emulating the spell \u201cCreate Truth\u201d (Prime 5, MtAw 170) with reach for advanced duration. This ritual takes an hour to complete. While most forge masters create hallows near where they do their craft there is nothing saying they must, by now they have the magical experience to know the consequences of such an action.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Matter 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The creations of the forge masters become like their children and with this final attainment they can give them a semblance of life, the ability to heal. After an hour of working on the structure or object they wish to repair they emulate the \u201cSelf-Repairing Machine\u201d (Matter 5, MtAw 159) spell with reach for advanced duration. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soul Forgers</span></span></span></b></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An offshoot of the Forge Masters, the Soul Forgers also believe in the importance of creation, perfection, and truth, but they take a different approach. They continue to maintain the normal work of their fellow legacy members, but they also study the refinement and perfection of the soul. Generally their soul is what they wish to perfect, but in order to interact with their own soul they must master the Death arcanum, the legacy, or engage in other powerful magics, therefore the occasional Soul Forger turns to reaping. In fact if the Pentacle discovered the existence of this legacy they would label them reapers, even if the mage never reaped a sleeper soul. It should be noted that this is not a separate legacy from the forge masters, only a subset of them with different optional attainments. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Death 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first attainment Soul Forgers learn allows them to gain basic information on their soul. The attainment functions as \u201cSoul Marks\u201d (Death 1. MtAw 128) with reach for instant casting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Death 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to study their soul they must protect it. This attainment takes an hour to activate and emulates \u201cSoul Armor\u201d (Death 2, MtAw 129) with reach for advanced duration. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Alternative Death 2</span> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some soul forgers know early on their intent to use the souls of others in their research and they design an attainment that stores the souls they plan to steal. This attainment functions as \u201cSoul Jar\u201d (Death 2, MtAw 129) with reach for advanced duration. It takes one hour to prepare the soul jar.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Death 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most of the soul forgers continue down the traditional path of their legacy here, gaining the 3rd and 4th optional attainments like any other powersmith. Unfortunately not all soul forgers are on a just path. Those who have foul experiments in mind for their own souls wish to begin testing the souls of others before the time comes to smelt their own. This attainment functions as \u201cSever Soul\u201d (Death 3, MtAw 132) with reach for advanced duration. In order to activate this attainment it takes an hour-long ritual that at a minimum causes harm, physically and psychologically, to their non-awakened victim.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Death 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As they continue down their path of reaping the destruction of a soul becomes inevitable, however they don\u2019t do so without benefit to themselves, instead the destruction of a soul allows them to relinquish spells safely as \u201cReaping Relinquishment\u201d (Death 3, SoS 73) with reach for instant casting and advanced duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Death 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The soul forger's optional capstone attainment finally allows the work on their own soul to be done without spells. This attainment functions as \u201cSever the Awakened Soul\u201d (Death 5, MtAw 133) with reach for advanced duration. The majority of soul forgers use this attainment just on their own soul and return it once whatever work they wish to do has been finished. Those who have been studying the refinement and perfection of the soul on sleepers might now decide that the souls of other awakened must first be studied, so as to not risk their own soul. The attainment takes an hour to activate. If used on your own soul it is uncomfortable but painless. If done on anyone else the psychological and physical trauma is immense. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 10-19-2023, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T19:45:35-08:00","id":1499344,"title":"","content":"<i><u><b>ANOTHER </b></u></i>legacy in a short amount of time but the inspiration hit me for one of my characters, who was already leaning towards Forge Masters, working to perfect his own soul, making the forge masters a Prime/Death legacy instead of Prime/Matter. So I did it. Couldn't not see some reapers coming out of this so I included that attainment path and because I had time this weekend I just did the full legacy, instead of just the Prime/Death side of it.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T23:06:15-08:00","id":1499351,"title":"","content":"Any particular reason you chose <u>Withering</u> over <u>Reaping Relinquishment</u>? Mechanically it's sound, but I'd have thought a craftsman Legacy would have prioritized maximizing the use of raw materials over direct offensive capabilities.<br /> <br /> Do you generally see the Golem as having &quot;crafting assistant&quot; as their purview, or does it change based on the activation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-11-2022, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T02:33:43-08:00","id":1499355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499343-powersmiths-forge-masters-23-conversion-soul-forgers-optional-death-sub-legacy?p=1499351#post1499351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular reason you chose <u>Withering</u> over <u>Reaping Relinquishment</u>? I'd have thought a craftsman Legacy would have prioritized maximizing the use of raw materials over direct offensive capabilities.<br /> <br /> Do you generally see the Golem as having &quot;crafting assistant&quot; as their purview, or does it change based on the activation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where do I find Reaping Relinquishment? I don't see it in core<br /> <br /> I see the golem mainly as an assistant to the work that the mage does yes, doing the more tedious things that a gnosis 6 (at least) mage can do but doesn't want to do, but each mage will come up with their own tasks for their golem. My character I can see having the golem do basic undergrad style lab work as he is a chemist for example, in addition to whatever work he is doing as a powersmith (assuming of course my character ever makes it to that attainment)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T02:57:06-08:00","id":1499356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499343-powersmiths-forge-masters-23-conversion-soul-forgers-optional-death-sub-legacy?p=1499355#post1499355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do I find Reaping Relinquishment? I don't see it in core</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry, it's in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>, page 73. The gist is you destroy a Soul (or a Soul Stone, with the Prime conjunctive effect) and safely Relinquish a spell without having to spend Willpower. Given that Attainments don't risk Hubris, that's a huge boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T03:04:25-08:00","id":1499357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499343-powersmiths-forge-masters-23-conversion-soul-forgers-optional-death-sub-legacy?p=1499356#post1499356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, sorry, it's in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>, page 73. The gist is you destroy a Soul (or a Soul Stone, with the Prime conjunctive effect) and safely Relinquish a spell without having to spend Willpower. Given that Attainments don't risk Hubris, that's a huge boon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh that, that's really big and and makes sense, I'll look at it and port it over","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T03:08:34-08:00","id":1499358,"title":"","content":"Amoral as hell, but it fits the skill-set you get already given them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T03:14:32-08:00","id":1499359,"title":"","content":"Made that change, like that so much better tyvm for pointing it out to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}